  - language: 10
    solidName: Dodecahedron
    solidFamily: Platonic Solid
    description: Twelve pentagons joined in a cosmic symmetry that represents the
      most intricate of the ancient Greek elements.
    fact1: Dual polyhedron of the icosahedron.
    fact2: Plato associated it with the shape of the universe in the Timaeus.
    fact3: It has exactly 160 distinct internal diagonals connecting its 20 vertices.
    natureEntries:
    - title: Garnet crystals
      description: Some garnet varieties grow with pentagonal dodecahedral faces.
      category: 2
    - title: Cosmic large-scale structure
      description: A 2003 study suggested the universe may have dodecahedral topology.
      category: 3
    - title: Acoustic Engineering
      description: Speakers in this shape are used to measure acoustics,  sound radiates
        equally in every direction.
      category: 0
